course: dictionary
lesson: 3889
title: Frequently and its friends
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Frequently means often, or many times. When you meet it, ask yourself: how many times does this happen? «New meanings often come from technology, jokes, stories and slang, and the old meaning frequently lives on beside the new one.» The writer uses often and then frequently, so the two words mean much the same thing.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. The old meaning lives on beside the new one again and again, not just once. Now swap in your meaning: «the old meaning often lives on beside the new one» still makes sense, so frequently means often.
explain: Frequently is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens. It can change form: more frequently means more often, and most frequently means the most often. You will meet it in maths and science, and in exams, where it is a more formal word than often.
fact: Frequently means often, or many times.
fact: More frequently means more often; most frequently means the most often.
fact: In statistics, the mode is the value that appears most frequently in a set of data.
fact: FAQ stands for frequently asked questions, the questions people ask most often.
fact: Frequently is a stiffer, more formal word than often, so formal texts and exams often use it.
exercise: «The old meaning frequently lives on beside the new one.» What does frequently mean here? | Once, long ago | Never at all | *Often, many times | Very quickly
exercise: Sam writes in a class survey: «Pizza is the food chosen most frequently.» What does most frequently mean? | Only once | Very quickly | The least often | *The most often
exercise: «New meanings often come from technology, jokes, stories and slang.» Which word in this sentence means the same as frequently? | slang | new | *often | meanings
test: Which word means the same as frequently? | Rarely | Slowly | *Often | Never
test: Ali says the bus is late ____ on Mondays. Which formal word fits best? | Finally | Hardly | *Frequently | Quietly
exam: What does FAQ stand for on a website? | Final answer query | *Frequently asked questions | Fun and Quick | Free after quiz
